    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d435">

                <pb facs="0517" n="505" sameAs="frus:frus1941v02/pg505"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">851.4016/33: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Germany</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Morris</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-05-10T18:00:00+02:00">May 10, 1941—6
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 6:40 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1829. The DNB<anchor n="64" xml:id="d435-f1"/> reports that in discussing the
                    latest measures to exclude Jews from economic life in Paris it was stated by
                    “competent German quarters” there that it is desired to obtain a “uniform
                    settlement of the Jewish question as an international problem” and that <pb
                        facs="0518" n="506" xml:id="pg506"/> “a final settlement for all Europe will
                    be made with the conclusion of peace”.</p>
                <p>It has been apparent for some time that a systematic plan is being directed from
                    Berlin to establish in all countries under its control the German discrimination
                    against Jews as rapidly as the local situation permits. The first step is in
                    each case exclusion from political activity followed by social ostracism and
                    economic despoliation leading ultimately to compulsory labor, forced emigration
                    and ghettoization.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Morris</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
